  "duration_semantics": "Owned speech and action slots determine sequence runtime. Direction coverage applies to existing following moments and never adds time by itself. Coverage spans and overlap intersections must not be added to runtime.",
  "direction_association_semantics": "Each direction starts at its authored script position. Source and speech associations retain context only. Coverage begins at that fixed anchor and can extend forward through following entries; affecting earlier words requires moving the direction earlier in the script.",
  "relationship_to_approved_main": "The earlier approved main remains the visual reference. The proposed main retains one script flow and one common text edge. Direction coverage shares a single vertical gutter track with distinct colors and interleaved overlap strokes. Fixed tops curve right into arrows pointing to their own direction lines; only the selected lower/end handle resizes forward coverage. Speech uses ordinary duration pills. The Storyboard retains spoken-word pills, marquee selection and direction coverage bands.",
